## Context

Author decision, 2026-11-10, in a harness session on the documentary chain
(harness tickets 1502 and 1503): "Okay to change DOIfetch output to docs/",
then "that was the permission to change DOIfetch defaults. But don't rely on
it, use explicit --output-dir".

The author's projects stage every source document in a git-ignored `docs/`
folder before it is archived in Zotero (harness `rules/zotero.md`: fetch,
stage in `docs/`, archive). DOIfetch writes to `papers/` by default
(`src/doifetch/config.py:40`, `PAPERS_DIR = "papers"`; `--output-dir` in
`src/doifetch/cli.py:158`; README tree at line 123), so a file fetched
without the option lands outside the staging folder.

The harness does not depend on this change: it runs DOIfetch at a pinned tag
and, from its ticket 1503 on, always passes `--output-dir` explicitly.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The default output directory is `docs`; `--output-dir` still overrides it
- [ ] README and the CLI help describe the new default; a note says the old default was `papers`
- [ ] A test shows a fetch with no `--output-dir` writing under `docs/`
- [ ] The project's own gate passes
